From b0b6fb0135b9e416627085c8f0e873d4c59a8ce2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: writer <writer@local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:29:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] P15A.1 Wave 2 (b): the shared-market root joins the
 Save45 step (1361-E2 r2)

1355-A sections 3.3 to 3.5 and section 8 item 5, commit (b), through
the slice 2a extension points (1361-F rulings 3 to 6):
- src/core/marketIntegration.ts: the root's empty form, its named
  accessor, and validateSharedMarketRoot: exact keys and version,
  ranges, each row's fields, its known definition and the phase triple
  of its own phaseOrderVersion read through the P15_PHASE_TABLES export,
  strict (week, releaseId) and sequence ascent, no row without an
  industry, the film bijection, and the law reconciled week by week by
  era. No private allocator check (1361-F ruling 5).
- types.ts: PersistedMarketAssessment, SharedMarketRoot, and
  sharedMarket in P15StepRoots, so GameStateV45 carries it.
- save.ts: sharedMarket in the P15_ROOT_KEYS literal, so its satisfies
  clause against P15StepRoots holds (1361-F3 R1), and in
  P15_SEQUENCED_ROOTS; the market refusal first in
  P15_DOWNGRADE_REFUSALS; the empty root in
  initialP15Roots (fresh worlds, migration, the historical lift), and
  the market validator in validateSaveV45 before the one allocator
  check.
- historical-control.ts: the hash discards only an empty market root.
- tick.ts: no batch runs in this commit, so a world with an industry
  keeps its root recording from the week each advance produces. Every
  state this commit writes satisfies the full validator, and a save it
  writes loads under commit (c) with the disclosed ramp.

No economic change: no reception reads the root, and the seam stays at 1.

r2: F3 guard (1361-D2 finding F3; 1361-F4 ruling 3 item 4). Before the
finalize write moves recordedFromWeek, tick() refuses by name when the
sharedMarket root already holds a row: such a save was written by a
build with the market batch, and this build cannot move recordedFromWeek
past those rows. A (c)-era save opened in a (b)-only build now fails at
its first tick instead of at the next save.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
